'' AN ENUM TO A POINTER, AND A NULL POINTER CONSTANT TO AN INTEGER, compile and link.
'' fbc accepts both with a warning -- 1, 'passing scalar as pointer', and 2 -- and writes
'' '(struct $1T*)E1$0' and 'F( 0 )'. tiko scored the only candidate unviable, left the
'' call untyped and dropped the statement. See the source and src/symbols/argmismatch.bas
'' (ArgShapeCost_).
''
'' A DRIVER TEST BECAUSE IT HAS TO LINK: --dump-ir stops before the emitter, and this
'' file's first draft passed '0 statements not lowered' while clang refused its IR. The
'' source is also a goldenrun.sh differential: built and run by fbc and by tiko, the two
'' outputs are byte-identical (measured).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/driver/src/enum-nullptr-args.bas -o tests/driver/enumnullargs.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/enumnullargs.exe
